+	// cleared -- clearing it stops new transfers from being queued, it doesn't
+	// abort ones already in flight. Some drivers (e.g. the CD32 FMV cartridge's,
+	// which uses this same continuous/PBX streaming path to feed its cdmpeg
+	// player) disable streaming right after requesting one last batch of PBX
+	// slots and then wait for their RXDMADONE/PBX completion interrupts before
+	// considering the drive idle. Bailing out here as soon as CDFLAG_ENABLE goes
+	// low left those last slots undelivered -- no data, no interrupt, no error --
+	// which could stall a driver waiting on that completion.
