+	// also stream through this same PBX path for plain data loading (confirmed by
+	// instrumenting Flink's boot, which hits this same miss condition a handful of
+	// times during its own loading, harmlessly). The FMV cartridge is the one piece
+	// of hardware that actually needs faster-than-real-time PBX bursts (CDXL/cdmpeg
+	// streaming), so restrict the new behavior to when it is present; without the
+	// cartridge this is byte-for-byte the old code path, which keeps every non-FMV
+	// CD32 game's frame timing and savestate/replay compatibility untouched.
+	if (currprefs.cs_cd32fmv && (!(sector_buffer_sector_1 >= 0 && sec >= 0 && sec < SECTOR_BUFFER_SIZE) || sector_buffer_info_1[sec] == 0)) {
+		sched_yield();
